{"before":{"id":"fad661ba-5f17-4cec-b90e-0399ed007209","word":"before","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"in advance of the time when","word":"antes de"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"rather or sooner than","word":"antes que"}],"pos":"conj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Near-synonym: no later than","id":"2f6ba594-d53f-4b1a-a956-71e8eecb9b6b"},{"text":"Brush your teeth before you go to bed.","bold_text_offsets":[[17,23]],"type":"example","id":"00d90302-09a9-4603-ac6d-91b6b89066ab"},{"text":"But before this elaborate treatise can become of universal use and ornament to my native country, two points[…] are absolutely necessary.","ref":"1731 (date written), Simon Wagstaff [pseudonym; Jonathan Swift], “An Introduction to the Following Treatise”, in A Complete Collection of Genteel and Ingenious Conversation, […], London: […] B[enjamin] Motte […], published 1738, →OCLC, page xiv:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[4,10]],"id":"7a6d0e41-a1ea-4715-bba1-0d7be985082b"},{"text":"Stephen Ward then had to time his tackle excellently to deny Tarmo Kink as the Wolves winger slid the ball out of play before the Estonian could attempt to beat Given.","ref":"2011 November 11, Rory Houston, “Estonia 0-4 Republic of Ireland”, in RTE Sport:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[119,125]],"id":"1042a790-d45f-4ec3-a6c1-3a47fb88b7e1"}],"antonyms":[{"word":"after"}],"synonyms":[{"word":"no later than"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","English terms with usage examples"],"glosses":["In advance of the time when."],"id":"d2b9ab26-3deb-43cd-b1a4-10c2593c09c5"},{"examples":[{"text":"I'll die before I('ll) tell you anything about it.","bold_text_offsets":[[9,15]],"type":"example","id":"aafb6fb4-9bb1-48ea-85b2-f8932db2ebf9"}],"senseid":["en:indicating preferences"],"categories":["English informal terms","English terms with usage examples"],"links":[["Rather","rather"],["sooner","sooner"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"as soon as"}],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"no sooner than"},{"word":"lest"}],"raw_glosses":["(informal) Rather or sooner than."],"glosses":["Rather or sooner than."],"tags":["informal"],"id":"0dd768e1-cb08-499e-baff-4eefb222499a"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"before dark":{"id":"eb92e5e1-3cff-4fbe-bfde-71ad839fe10d","word":"before dark","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"before night begins to fall","word":"antes de anoitecer"},{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"before night begins to fall","word":"antes do cair da noite"}],"pos":"prep_phrase","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"I think you should finish mowing the lawn before dark.","bold_text_offsets":[[42,53]],"type":"example","id":"848738db-1c79-4e53-8003-3080a06fa84b"}],"links":[["night","night"]],"coordinate_terms":[{"word":"after dark"},{"word":"at dark"},{"word":"before dawn"}],"glosses":["Before night begins to fall."],"categories":["English entries with incorrect language header","English lemmas","English multiword terms","English prepositional phrases","English terms with usage examples","Entries with translation boxes","Pages with 1 entry","Pages with entries","Terms with Dutch translations","Terms with Finnish translations","Terms with French translations","Terms with German translations","Terms with Greek translations","Terms with Italian translations","Terms with Japanese translations","Terms with Korean translations","Terms with Latin translations","Terms with Mandarin translations","Terms with Polish translations","Terms with Portuguese translations","Terms with Russian translations","Terms with Serbo-Croatian translations","Terms with Spanish translations"],"id":"d769233e-0686-4cd5-9369-376f39c386fa"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"befoul":{"id":"3976ed04-9f6a-4c01-ba6d-5305d364c57f","word":"befoul","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to make foul, to soil","word":"conspurcar"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"These heights are a desirable retreat, for less picturesque reasons—as an escape from a compound of vile smells perpetually arising from a great harbour full of stagnant water, and befouled by the refuse of innumerable ships with all sorts of cargoes: which, in hot weather, is dreadful in the last degree.","ref":"1846, Charles Dickens, “Avignon to Genoa”, in Pictures from Italy, London: […] Bradbury & Evans, […], →OCLC, page 34:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[181,189]],"id":"43631a2b-53df-4367-a03c-b79708a06600"},{"text":"1897, Robert Gwynneddon Davies (translator), The Sleeping Bard by Ellis Wynne, London: Simplkon, Marshall & Co., Part I,\nAt last, what with a round of blasphemy, and the whole crowd with clay pistols belching smoke and fire and slander of their neighbours, and the floor already befouled with dregs and spittle, I feared lest viler deeds should happen, and craved to depart.","id":"893c0325-d79a-4de9-9c23-f8834c967c77"},{"text":"Only the four walls of his home still stood, blackened and smoking with the sluggish, stinking smoke that befouled the sea-wind.","ref":"1983, Mary Stewart, chapter 5, in The Wicked Day, New York: William Morrow, page 53:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[106,114]],"id":"b7ef4541-59fc-4ed9-a8d6-fc3757f66c16"},{"text":"1997, Ted Hughes, Tales from Ovid, “Echo and Narcissus” in Paul Keegan (ed.), Ted Hughes: Collected Poems, New York: Farrar, Straus and Giroux, 2003, p. 919,\nThere was a pool of perfect water.\n[…] No cattle\nHad slobbered their muzzles in it\nAnd befouled it.","id":"7c442291-4a1c-4159-a03d-50057f3dab65"}],"links":[["foul","foul"],["soil","soil"],["contaminate","contaminate"],["pollute","pollute"]],"synonyms":[{"word":"befile"},{"word":"befilth"},{"word":"foul"},{"word":"assoil","source":"Thesaurus:dirty","tags":["obsolete"]},{"word":"beclart","source":"Thesaurus:dirty","tags":["UK","dialectal"]},{"word":"bedaub","source":"Thesaurus:dirty","tags":